OL,3,GNEWSAGrand National winner continues to
OL,4,Achampion cancer research
OL,5,
OL,6,FEighteen months before Bob Champion won
OL,7,Fthe Grand National in 1981, he was told
OL,8,Fhe only had four months to live after
OL,9,Fbeing diagnosed with testicular cancer
OL,10,Fwhich had spread to his lungs.
OL,12,FSince then, Champion, who lives in
OL,13,FNewmarket, Suffolk, has raised more
OL,14,Fthan #17m through his cancer trust,
OL,15,Fwhich he established in 1983.
OL,17,FAfter undergoing treatment for bladder
OL,18,Fcancer earlier this year, he is
OL,19,Fdetermined to continue fundraising for
OL,20,Fcancer research.
OL,23,APub: 07-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
